# Tooltip Final Render Hooks Implementation Plan

## Status

Phases 0 through 6 complete. This document is the execution contract for
rendering the current process-wide tooltip intent after its owning native
overlay or Lua screen has completed rendering.

It depends on the polling, detection, and intent contracts in
`Docs/tooltip-input-polling.todo`. It does not replace or absorb any input
responsibility from that plan.

## Goal

Present the current DwarfUI tooltip:

- after the complete base-game viewscreen render,
- after every DFHack overlay rendered by `plugins.overlay`,
- after the complete content of a Lua `gui.Screen` or `gui.ZScreen` that owns
  the tooltip target,
- without creating a `gui.ZScreen`,
- without registering an `OverlayWidget`,
- without receiving, forwarding, or consuming input,
- without participating in viewscreen focus or logic, and
- without allowing a tooltip failure to break normal overlay or Lua-screen
  rendering.

The implementation will select one of two render transports from the intent's
opaque `source_root`:

- Native and `OverlayWidget` roots use a runtime wrapper around the exported
  `plugins.overlay.render_viewscreen_widgets()` function.
- Lua `gui.Screen` and `gui.ZScreen` roots use an on-demand wrapper around the
  effective `onRender()` method on that exact screen instance.

Both wrappers call the function they replaced first and then offer the current
`TooltipIntent` to one shared presenter.

## Supported presentation boundary

The initial implementation supports:

- tooltip targets rendered in the native viewscreen and DFHack overlay
  pipeline, including the native Hauling menu and DwarfUI minecart overlay;
- tooltip targets rooted in a displayed Lua `gui.Screen` or `gui.ZScreen`,
  including classes that override `onRender()`; and
- nested Lua-screen stacks, with presentation restricted to the current top
  screen.

The render system does not patch `gui.Screen.onRender` globally. It wraps the
effective method on the target's actual root instance so a class-specific
override is preserved and unrelated screens are untouched.

An unsupported root is one that is neither eligible for the native overlay
pipeline nor a displayed Lua screen with a callable `onRender()` method. Such
an intent produces no painting and an explicit diagnostic reason.

## Scope boundary

This plan owns:

- runtime installation of the native-overlay render trampoline,
- on-demand installation of Lua-screen instance render trampolines,
- safe chaining with the function already exported by `plugins.overlay`,
- safe chaining with the effective `onRender()` method already installed on a
  target screen instance,
- same-version reload and module-replacement behavior,
- screen dismissal and garbage-collection behavior,
- exactly-once tooltip presentation through the transport selected by the
  current source root,
- consumption of `TooltipIntent` notifications,
- redraw invalidation,
- tooltip measurement, placement, and painting,
- supported-surface filtering,
- failure isolation and diagnostics,
- focused, full-suite, package, and live evidence.

This plan does not own:

- pointer sampling or hit testing,
- tooltip registration or hover callbacks,
- tooltip-text validation,
- input forwarding or consumption,
- overlay update callbacks,
- viewscreen focus, raising, dismissal, or logic,
- modification of DFHack's installed `plugins/overlay.lua` source,
- global ordering against unrelated code that deliberately patches itself
  outside DwarfUI after the last tooltip intent update,
- decoration of Lua screens that do not own a registered tooltip target, or
- a universal engine-level post-compositor hook.

## Confirmed architecture

### Stable process state

Keep hook ownership in a versioned process-wide slot:

```lua
---@class dwarfui.TooltipRenderHookState
---@field api_version integer
---@field overlay_module table|nil
---@field overlay_hook dwarfui.TooltipRenderHookRecord|nil
---@field screen_hooks table<gui.Screen, dwarfui.TooltipRenderHookRecord>
---@field presenter function|nil
---@field generation integer
---@field render_count integer
---@field last_rendered_revision integer|nil
---@field last_transport dwarfui.TooltipRenderTransport|nil
---@field last_error string|nil
---@field disabled_generation integer|nil

---@class dwarfui.TooltipRenderHookRecord
---@field transport dwarfui.TooltipRenderTransport
---@field owner table|nil Strong overlay-module owner only.
---@field owner_ref table|nil Weak-value screen-owner reference only.
---@field active_trampoline function|nil
---@field predecessor function|nil
---@field owner_had_raw_method boolean|nil
---@field owner_raw_method function|nil
---@field generation integer
---@field repair_count integer
```

The slot belongs under `dfhack.dwarfui`. Same-version DwarfUI reloads update
the presenter generation in this stable state instead of relying on closures
from the cleared module environment. `screen_hooks` uses weak keys so hook
diagnostics and lifecycle tracking do not keep dismissed screens alive.

### Chained render trampolines

Transport identity uses the exported numeric
`dwarfui.TooltipRenderTransport` enum. Hook state, records, diagnostics, and
presenter callbacks never exchange string transport tags.

Each installed trampoline captures:

- the function installed immediately before it,
- its own function identity, and
- enough identity to find its current hook record in the stable process slot.

A screen hook additionally records whether `onRender` originally existed as a
raw instance field. Conditional restoration reinstates that raw value when it
existed and otherwise clears the trampoline field so normal class inheritance
resumes. It must not leave an inherited predecessor copied onto the instance
as a permanent shadow of later class updates.

Its behavior is:

1. Call the captured predecessor with the original arguments and preserve its
   return values.
2. Re-read the current hook state from `dfhack.dwarfui`.
3. Continue only if this trampoline is still active for its transport owner.
4. Verify that the current intent selects this transport and owner.
5. Invoke the current presenter generation through an error boundary.
6. Return the predecessor's original return values.

The predecessor call remains outside the tooltip error boundary. DwarfUI must
not reinterpret or suppress failures from DFHack's normal overlay renderer,
the target screen's original `onRender()`, or another wrapper in either
established chain.

### Transport selection

The presenter adapter classifies only the current intent's `source_root`:

- An eligible native or `OverlayWidget` root selects the global overlay
  trampoline.
- A displayed Lua screen with callable `_native` and `onRender` members selects
  that exact screen instance's trampoline.
- Every other root selects no transport and records an unsupported-root
  diagnostic.

The overlay trampoline must skip screen-owned intents. A screen trampoline must
skip unless:

- the intent's `source_root` is its exact owner,
- `dfhack.gui.getCurViewscreen(true)` is its owner's `_native`, and
- its trampoline is the active wrapper for that owner.

These checks prevent the native overlay hook or a lower parent screen from
painting an early tooltip that a foreground screen could subsequently cover.

### Chain ownership and repair

When the renderer receives a new or cleared intent, reloads, or explicitly
checks its installation, it verifies the selected transport:

- For the overlay transport, compare the exported
  `plugins.overlay.render_viewscreen_widgets` function with the active overlay
  trampoline.
- For the screen transport, compare `source_root.onRender` with that owner's
  active screen trampoline.
- If the corresponding function is already active, no change is required.
- If the current function is an ordinary wrapper whose function-upvalue chain
  retains the active DwarfUI trampoline, DwarfUI remains installed but is not
  outermost. Preserve the wrapper's ownership and exact restoration contract.
- A wrapper owner can explicitly mark its function reorderable through the
  hook manager. DwarfUI may repair above only that opted-in wrapper, allowing
  tooltip painting after the wrapper's post-render work.
- If the overlay module was replaced, install against the replacement module.
- If the current function no longer chains the active DwarfUI trampoline, wrap
  that true replacement and designate the new trampoline as active.

Older DwarfUI trampolines remain in the predecessor chain but observe that
they are no longer active and skip presentation. This allows true replacement
repair without drawing the tooltip more than once. Screen trampolines
belonging to a previous source root remain inert unless that exact screen
becomes the current intent owner again.

The system does not fight an unmarked extension for the exported slot.
Verification and permitted repair occur only at explicit lifecycle boundaries
and intent notifications. Diagnostics distinguish installed-in-chain from
outermost ownership and from a replacement that requires or permits repair.

### Presenter

The active presenter reads the current immutable `TooltipIntent` at render
time. Notification handlers request redraw and repair the hook, but do not
cache a second authoritative copy of the intent.

For a supported intent, the presenter:

1. Reads the current screen dimensions.
2. Creates a full-screen UI painter whose global coordinates match
   `dfhack.screen.getMousePos()`.
3. Applies the current tooltip wrapping and placement policy.
4. Renders the tooltip once.
5. Records the rendered revision in diagnostics.

For no intent, a stale intent, a transport-owner mismatch, an unsupported
source root, or a disabled presenter generation, it performs no painting.

### Existing renderer reuse

Retain `dwarfui.TooltipRenderer` as the visual implementation unless focused
characterization identifies a concrete incompatibility with the global
painter. The hook owns one renderer instance per presenter generation and maps
the current intent into:

```lua
renderer:set_tooltip(
    intent.text,
    intent.anchor_x,
    intent.anchor_y,
    full_screen_rect)
```

The renderer remains a plain widget. It is not added as a subview and is not
attached to a screen, overlay, or consumer root.

If the renderer's current parent invalidation behavior cannot be used without
a UI owner, move invalidation into the presenter notification adapter instead
of introducing a synthetic parent view.

## Ordering guarantees

The implementation guarantees:

- the selected predecessor render function completes before tooltip painting;
- all viewscreen-specific and `all` overlay widgets rendered by that
  predecessor are beneath an overlay-owned tooltip;
- all content drawn by a wrapped Lua screen's effective `onRender()` method is
  beneath that screen's tooltip;
- a lower Lua screen in a parent chain cannot present while another Lua screen
  is current;
- the overlay hook cannot present a screen-owned intent;
- older DwarfUI trampolines do not paint;
- one selected active trampoline paints at most once per completed owner
  render;
- an intent notification preserves a proven outer owner unless it explicitly
  permits reordering, and repairs a true replacement that no longer chains
  DwarfUI.

The implementation cannot guarantee:

- ordering after work performed by another extension's outer wrapper, even
  when that wrapper cooperatively calls DwarfUI in its predecessor chain;
- recognizing a wrapper that hides its predecessor outside the bounded
  function-and-table Lua upvalue graph available through `debug.getupvalue`;
- rendering on native viewscreen classes that the DFHack overlay plugin does
  not interpose;
- rendering above a Lua screen that does not own the tooltip target and is not
  represented by the intent's `source_root`;
- rendering after a target screen replaces its own `onRender()` after the last
  intent notification without another repair boundary; or
- ordering against native or external drawing that occurs after the selected
  predecessor returns.

These limitations must be documented and tested as scope boundaries rather
than hidden behind screen-type exception lists.

## Lifecycle decisions

- Install the global overlay hook when the tooltip presenter subscribes to the
  service, not from pointer polling code.
- Install a screen hook only when a current intent selects that exact screen
  root.
- Hook installation is valid before map load because it creates no viewscreen,
  widget, timeout, input handler, or logic callback.
- A missing current intent makes the active presenter a no-op.
- Intent publish and clear notifications repair hook ownership and request one
  redraw through a presentation-owned invalidation adapter.
- DwarfUI reload replaces the presenter generation and retires the prior
  renderer instance without nesting an active presentation callback.
- `plugins.overlay.rescan()` must not disturb the hook.
- Replacement or clearing of the `plugins.overlay` module is detected the next
  time installation is ensured.
- Screen hook records must not keep dismissed or otherwise unreachable screens
  alive.
- Intent transfer from one Lua screen to another repairs the new owner and
  makes the former owner's trampoline presentation-inert.
- Explicit shutdown clears the presenter and disables the active generation
  before attempting to restore the overlay or screen functions.
- Restore a predecessor only when its owner still exposes DwarfUI's exact
  active trampoline.
- Screen restoration must preserve whether the predecessor was instance-owned
  or inherited.
- If another wrapper is currently outermost, leave the corresponding inert
  DwarfUI trampoline in its predecessor chain rather than overwriting the other
  wrapper.
- A stale trampoline may call its predecessor but must never call a retired
  presenter.

## Failure-containment decisions

- Run only the DwarfUI presenter through `xpcall`.
- Never include an overlay or screen predecessor render call inside the tooltip
  `xpcall`.
- On presenter failure, capture a traceback, failed revision, generation, and
  transport-owner identity.
- Disable the failed presenter generation immediately.
- Log the failure once and suppress per-frame repetition.
- Leave both trampoline types and predecessor chains operational so normal
  overlays and Lua screens continue rendering.
- Require an explicit presenter replacement, repair command, or DwarfUI reload
  before a failed generation can render again.
- A malformed intent should fail within the presenter boundary and must not
  corrupt the process-wide input service state.

