- [x] Add a focused live probe proving that replacing
      `plugins.overlay.render_viewscreen_widgets` changes the function called
      by the native C++ overlay interpose hook.
- [x] Record the exact function arguments and return values received by the
      installed DFHack version.
- [x] Prove the wrapped predecessor renders viewscreen-specific overlays and
      `viewscreens='all'` overlays before the appended callback.
- [x] Prove the appended callback can paint a known cell above a native
      viewscreen and above both overlay groups.
- [x] Verify screen-global pointer coordinates align with a full-window
      `gui.Painter` in classic and graphics modes supported by the test
      environment.
- [x] Characterize the redraw API needed to show and clear appended painting
      immediately while the game is paused.
- [x] Verify `plugins.overlay.rescan()` preserves a runtime replacement of the
      exported render function.
- [x] Characterize behavior when the overlay Lua module environment is cleared
      and reloaded.
- [x] Confirm that a foreground `gui.ZScreen` paints after the native overlay
      hook.
- [x] Add a focused live probe that wraps the effective `onRender()` method on
      an actual displayed `gui.ZScreen` instance.
- [x] Prove the instance predecessor completes its parent render, frame,
      content, and child rendering before the appended callback paints.
- [x] Prove the C++ Lua-screen render path looks up the instance's current
      `onRender` field on every render instead of caching the original method.
- [x] Characterize a screen class that overrides `onRender()` and prove
      instance wrapping preserves and follows that override.
- [x] Characterize nested Lua screens and prove only the current top screen is
      eligible to present.
- [x] Prove assignment and conditional restoration of an instance
      `onRender()` method do not alter its focus, input, logic, dismissal, or
      parent relationships.

### Phase 0 characterization evidence

| Surface | Installed-version result |
| --- | --- |
| Native arguments | The C++ interpose calls the exported function with exactly `('viewscreen_dwarfmodest', native_viewscreen)` on the fortress screen. |
| Native returns | The installed predecessor returns no values; the wrapper preserves that empty return list. |
| Native ordering | The viewscreen-specific probe paints `V`, the `all` probe paints `A`, and the appended full-window painter paints `H` last through the real `dfhack.screen.paintTile` path. |
| Coordinates and mode | In the configured graphics-mode environment, `dfhack.screen.getMousePos()`, a full-window `gui.Painter`, and the real paint call agree on the same screen-global cell. The environment does not provide an automation-safe runtime switch to classic mode. |
| Paused redraw | `ds.redraw()` immediately shows the appended paint and restores the predecessor's `A` cell when appended painting is disabled while paused. |
| Rescan and reload | `plugins.overlay.rescan()` retains the replacement function. `reload('plugins.overlay')` retains the module-table identity but overwrites the exported function with a new module-generation function. |
| Screen ordering | The native overlay callback occurs inside `ZScreen:renderParent()` before frame, content, child, and class-specific override rendering; the instance callback then paints last. |
| Dynamic screen lookup | Replacing the displayed instance's `onRender` field is observed on the next render, with zero arguments and zero predecessor return values. |
| Nested screens | A lower screen still renders as a parent but fails the current-native identity check; only the current top screen is eligible to append paint. |
| Restoration and behavior | Raw instance ownership is restored exactly, including clearing an originally inherited method. Focus strings, input, idle logic, parents, and normal dismissal remain intact. |

