## Phase 5: Prove native and Lua-screen final rendering

- [x] Update the focused minecart tooltip `.ds.lua` test to use the actual
      registered minecart overlay and zoom button.
- [x] Open the native Hauling menu through public DwarfSpec input APIs.
- [x] Move the pointer onto the production zoom button and await the published
      `Zoom to this stop` intent.
- [x] Assert the tooltip is painted at the expected screen cells without any
      tooltip `ZScreen`.
- [x] Enable a controlled viewscreen-specific test overlay that paints a
      conflicting sentinel into the tooltip cells and prove the tooltip is
      final.
- [x] Enable a controlled `viewscreens='all'` test overlay that paints the same
      conflicting sentinel and prove the tooltip is final.
- [x] Install a controlled foreign render wrapper, repair on the next intent
      notification, and prove both wrappers execute while the tooltip remains
      final and appears exactly once.
- [x] Move the pointer off the button and prove the underlying native and
      overlay content is restored on the requested redraw.
- [x] Assert the native focus string, current viewscreen, pause state, and input
      routing do not change when the tooltip appears or clears.
- [x] Assert render-hook diagnostics report installed, outermost, one active
      presenter generation, and the expected rendered intent revision.
- [x] Run `dwarfui reload` while the Hauling menu remains open and prove the
      production overlay, poller, render hook, and tooltip all recover without
      duplication.
- [x] Add a foreground DwarfSpec `ZScreen` fixture containing a real registered
      tooltip control.
- [x] Give the fixture a class-specific `onRender()` implementation that paints
      a conflicting sentinel after rendering its parent and content.
- [x] Move the pointer onto that control and prove the instance screen hook
      paints the tooltip after the sentinel.
- [x] Stack a second DwarfSpec `ZScreen` above the wrapped fixture and prove the
      lower screen hook does not paint while it is not current.
- [x] Register a tooltip target on the upper screen and prove presentation
      transfers to the upper instance without the overlay hook or lower screen
      also painting.
- [x] Assert the wrapped screen's focus, current viewscreen identity, input
      delivery, logic cadence, parent relationship, and dismissal behavior are
      unchanged.
- [x] Run `dwarfui reload` while the foreground fixture remains open and prove
      its existing trampoline resolves the new presenter generation without
      duplicate painting.
- [x] Dismiss the wrapped screens and prove their weak hook records and test
      subjects are released.
- [x] Restore the original exported overlay render function, every wrapped
      screen method, controlled test overlays, pointer, Hauling state, focus,
      and mounted DwarfSpec subjects even when an assertion fails.
- [x] Require `cleanup_confirmed=true` and zero retained DwarfSpec screens,
      subjects, pointer ownership, test overlays, screen wrappers, or foreign
      wrappers.

